Package: msamodel
Type: Package
Title: Mutation-Stability-Activity Model of Neutral Structural Evolution
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Julian", "Echave", email = "jechave@unsam.edu.ar",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Mathilde", "Carpentier", role = "aut"))
Description: Implementation of the Mutation-Stability-Activity (MSA) model for
    predicting site-specific structural divergence in protein evolution from
    single-point-mutation scans (SPMs). Provides maximum-likelihood estimation of
    the two selection-strength parameters with delta-method standard errors,
    prediction of divergence profiles under mutation-only and selection-only model
    variants, and a decomposition of the profile into mutation, stability, and
    activity contributions. Profiles are reported on two axes: per residue and per
    normal mode.
